    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Databricks, founded in 2013 and headquartered in San Francisco, CA, describes itself as a provider of a unified platform for data, analytics, and AI aimed at enterprise customers. The company's site positions its offering around what it calls a \"lakebase,\" described as a unified transactional layer that ties together data, AI, and governance to support building, deploying, and managing production applications on a single platform. Its stated capabilities span ETL, data warehousing, governance, and AI agent development, as well as a business intelligence layer the company calls Genie, which it describes as enabling natural language dashboard creation and conversational analytics.\n\nOn the AI product side, Databricks offers DBRX, an open-source large language model built on a Mixture-of-Experts architecture and positioned for enterprise use. The broader Databricks AI platform incorporates MLflow for model governance and Unity Catalog for data governance and lineage tracking, reflecting a data-centric approach to AI development. The site frames the platform as oriented toward helping organizations build production-ready AI agents grounded in their own data.\n\nThe held facts confirm Databricks is a for-profit startup with an active presence on theworldofai.org. No litigation, MCP server registrations, or SEC filings are recorded for the company in the current dataset.",
